{"id": "EUVD-2026-95539", "enisaUuid": "a6c0f097-82d5-30b8-8362-af2149a56096", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Fix out-of-bounds read of sk_protocol in bpf_sock_destroy()\n\nsk_protocol lives in struct sock, not in struct sock_common. A timewait\nor request sock handed to bpf_sock_destroy() by the tcp iterator is\nneither, so reading sk->sk_protocol runs past the object:\n\n==================================================================\nBUG: KASAN: slab-out-of-bounds in bpf_sock_destroy+0xc7/0xe0\nRead of size 2 at addr ffff8881047d11b4 by task test_progs/428\n\nTainted: [W]=WARN\nCall Trace:\n <TASK>\n dump_stack_lvl+0x91/0xf0\n print_report+0xd1/0x630\n kasan_report+0xf3/0x130\n __asan_report_load2_noabort+0x14/0x30\n bpf_sock_destroy+0xc7/0xe0\n bpf_prog_c3dd61f9d9cd9f37_iter_tcp6_timewait+0x9f/0xb7\n bpf_iter_run_prog+0x538/0xde0\n bpf_iter_tcp_seq_show+0x26b/0x4b0\n bpf_seq_read+0x424/0x1210\n vfs_read+0x197/0xe40\n ksys_read+0x119/0x240\n __x64_sys_read+0x72/0xc0\n x64_sys_call+0x647/0x27e0\n do_syscall_64+0xe5/0x610\n entry_SYSCALL_64_after_hwframe+0x76/0x7e\n\nOnly check sk_protocol on full socks. tcp_abort() already knows how to\ndeal with TIME_WAIT and NEW_SYN_RECV socks. Also fix the comment, it\nnever matched the code.", "datePublished": "2026-10-09T07:34:23", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:18:35", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5b4eb82475ae17d55974235c09e97044829426a8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a9651704c6fd64590b5ad4fbe7c3768accf95993", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/91a482a81eabddebf5430cbbdf12027e1a91b767", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2534a5e5d360c2b10203cfa80f4ab9d021e48f2f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/01b245ba016d44861690594e10f67e026ce8552f"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98384", "GHSA-rjxf-mj66-7hpg"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2c8e4295-46b0-323b-9b2d-d65a35e4fd3e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4ddbcb886268af8d12a23e6640b39d1d9c652b1b <5b4eb82475ae17d55974235c09e97044829426a8"}, {"id": "49c54e0b-b4a1-369c-b23e-1ccfea6c3bb5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.5"}, {"id": "4b2d2615-6bc0-38a7-bd12-37e2dd2181e4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "767eac4c-8f08-315a-8f42-ddb112151f92", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "851d146f-d27f-3940-8c48-09c52cb6d953", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4ddbcb886268af8d12a23e6640b39d1d9c652b1b <a9651704c6fd64590b5ad4fbe7c3768accf95993"}, {"id": "8b42faca-cbaf-3ec1-9268-429721110de4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "8c8a79c3-1831-3001-a039-fe970daf8703", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "9267cff6-48ee-3fde-9dc5-18c40189f1d0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4ddbcb886268af8d12a23e6640b39d1d9c652b1b <01b245ba016d44861690594e10f67e026ce8552f"}, {"id": "a922a7d0-4a87-3fa7-9819-dc9418fd1b5b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4ddbcb886268af8d12a23e6640b39d1d9c652b1b <2534a5e5d360c2b10203cfa80f4ab9d021e48f2f"}, {"id": "d0895554-0eaa-3eb1-a8dd-858dae84cf5e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "daf5ea20-f068-3c21-8ced-a4c4cd95bba9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "debc27d1-b26a-3278-b50b-a55549b97d45", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4ddbcb886268af8d12a23e6640b39d1d9c652b1b <91a482a81eabddebf5430cbbdf12027e1a91b767"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "71ac550a-a